# ============================================================================
# The root .env is NO LONGER used by docker compose for config (2026-07-14).
# All service config lives in env/*.env, loaded via `env_file:` in docker-compose.yml:
#   env/app.env          app behaviour · feature flags · model tiers · universe · knobs
#   env/gemini.env       GOOGLE_API_KEY (the one Gemini key)
#   env/data-keys.env    data-source API keys (OpenDART · ECOS · FRED · FMP · KIS · KRX · …)
#   env/auth-billing.env social login · email OTP · Toss billing · alert channels
#   env/secrets.env      generated secrets + admin login (AUTH_SECRET · SERVICE_TOKEN ·
#                        ADMIN_TOKEN · ADMINUI_USERNAME/PASSWORD/IP_ALLOWLIST · …)
#
# Set up:
#   for f in env/*.env.example; do cp "$f" "${f%.example}"; done   # then fill them in
#   # already have a monolithic .env?  bash scripts/split_env.sh   # → writes env/*.env by topic
#
# Each env/*.env.example is the annotated reference for its variables.
# ============================================================================
#
# The ONE thing that is NOT in env/*.env: the admin console's host port bind.
# A host port publish is compose-level, so `env_file:` can't provide it — docker compose
# interpolates ${ADMIN_BIND} in `ports:` only from the SHELL/CLI (or, if present, this root
# .env). It defaults to loopback (127.0.0.1, SC-0.2 — the console has CRUD over every DB).
# To expose it, pass it on the command line (no root .env needed):
#     ADMIN_BIND=0.0.0.0 docker compose up -d admin
# then gate it: cloud firewall + ADMINUI_IP_ALLOWLIST (env/secrets.env) + a strong
# ADMINUI_PASSWORD. Or set it here if you prefer a file:
# ADMIN_BIND=0.0.0.0
